invariant_date_columns_quoted: the builder keeps quotes as part of the
column name, so a quoted name in :INVARIANTDATECOLUMNS matches no column.
Each string-literal name warns on its span; the bare name between them is
silent.
-- input.ds --
:INVARIANTDATECOLUMNS := "booked_on", returned_on, 'due_on';
:PARAMETERS sMember := "";
SELECT booked_on, returned_on, due_on FROM loan WHERE member_code = @sMember
-- format --
:INVARIANTDATECOLUMNS := "booked_on", returned_on, 'due_on';
:PARAMETERS sMember := "";
SELECT booked_on, returned_on, due_on FROM loan WHERE member_code = @sMember
-- diagnostics --
1:26-1:37 warning invariant_date_columns_quoted: ':INVARIANTDATECOLUMNS' takes bare column names; the quotes are kept as part of the name, so it matches no column
1:52-1:60 warning invariant_date_columns_quoted: ':INVARIANTDATECOLUMNS' takes bare column names; the quotes are kept as part of the name, so it matches no column
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
